    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0753" n="683" xml:id="pg683"/>

                <head>No. 419.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Romero to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexican Legation in the United States</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 7, 1883</date>.
                        (Received February 10.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: I have the honor herewith to send
                    you a copy of a communication which I have this day received from the consul of
                    Mexico at Tombstone, Ariz., bearing date of the 24th of January last, whereby he
                    informs me that parties of Apaches have been leaving the San Carlos Reservation
                    in that Territory for the purpose of invading the State of Sonora, and that it
                    has thus far been impossible to get a stop put to these movements by the regular
                    forces of the United States.</p>
                <p>I think it proper to call your attention to this matter, pending the receipt of
                    instructions on the subject from the Mexican Government.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>M. ROMERO.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d420-a1.xml" xpointer="d420-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
